<PageTitle>dhcpr — no-log DNS</PageTitle>

<h1>A no-log DNS server, focused on privacy.</h1>
<p class="lead">
    DHCPR answers a DNS query and does not keep a history of it.
    The log records errors only. A lookup that succeeds is not written down.
</p>

<LandingQueryCount />

<h2>Public resolvers</h2>
<p class="lead">
    The same software is the public DNS service at these two names.
    Each one speaks classic DNS, DNS-over-TLS, and DNS-over-HTTPS.
</p>
